Akol in Armidale
Her dream of medicine has not gone anywhere. It has recalibrated. A year of steady work, a 
baby, a driving licence in progress, TAFE registration underway: the foundation is being built 
carefully, and nursing is what she is moving towards. 
When asked what she would say to newly arrived migrants who feel too uncertain or too afraid 
to a  sk for help, Akol answered without hesitation. 
"Don't   feel   shy.   Don't   feel   intimidated.   Come   out,   speak   to   someone  at   Mosaic. 
Everything remains private. Because if you are at home and you are having an issue, will 
anybody  know?  No.  But  if  you  come  out  and  talk  about  it,  they  will  know.  You  will  be 
helped and you will feel secure. Mosaic opens the door and you follow them." — Akol Koor 
Akol is one of many people rebuilding their lives in regional Australia with the right support at 
the right time. 
Since opening our Armidale office in 2019, Mosaic has supported 743 clients across 1,264 
cases. 
In 2025-26  alone, we worked with 159 clients across 337 cases, helping people move from 
uncertainty to stability, opportunity and belonging.